{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1220396-taking-a-bane-is-it-ever-worthwhile","id":1220396,"title":"Taking a Bane.is it ever worthwhile?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-19T19:18:24-07:00","id":1220396,"title":"Taking a Bane.is it ever worthwhile?","content":"As I understand it, if I take a bane I gain a new curse, on top of the Kindred conditions allready manifold curses<br /> <br /> AND take a -1 to all degeneration rolls in the future, that to me is a bigger deal<br /> <br /> is it really worth it to be exempted from rolling for degeneration for one particular breaking point?<br /> <br /> Can anyone show me why it's worthwhile<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T19:51:38-07:00","id":1220402,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness, on Beaten Down and Surrender:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These rules only apply to people who would incur a break- ing point for committing (or attempting) \u201cmurder.\u201d Creatures that don\u2019t have a problem killing people in general can ignore surrender without penalty and don\u2019t have the fight beaten out of them like normal folks. </div> </div> </div>Taking a Bane for \u201cpremeditated killing\u201d (i.e. murder), then, can be interpreted as making the character immune to the Beaten Down Tilt and able to freely ignore surrender.<br /> <br /> Additionally, it can be worth taking a Bane for a Breaking Point you expect to experience particularly often. For example, \u201cimpassioned violence\u201d would be a good one for any character that is likely to participate in combat. A reclusive elder might consider taking one for \u201cone month without human contact.\u201d<br /> <br /> Also, the supernatural weaknesses of the Banes themselves are usually not too obtrusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T04:17:47-07:00","id":1220497,"title":"","content":"If you plan on playing an unregenerate asshole or a high covenant status Dragon, yes it\u2019s worth it. The banes themselves are laughably ignorable to virtually nonexistent for Dragons with the right mysteries. (Your bane assigns a social penalty? Majesty or Nightmare fixes that. Your bane deals bashing damage? Resilience fixes that.) What\u2019s a -1 to -3 to degeneration checks if you don\u2019t make them because you baned out the activities you would be making checks repeatedly like torture, manslaughter, murder and have touchstones to offset the penalty if you do make a check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-20-2018, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T13:57:07-07:00","id":1220617,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, taking Banes works best the more extreme your Humanity. High Humanity vampires get dinged a lot, but the penalty is easily compensated for by Touchstones (and you want multiples for high Humanity characters anyway) and protecting your Dirge (also part of how you'd already be doing things), and they get a lot of Beats for all the minor stuff they get dinged for, easily offsetting the few failures they're suffer. A Bane or two helps make sure that things that are just bound to happen more than once if a vampire lives long enough (as noted impassioned violence is one of those) don't screw up the high Humanity Beats cycle. As well, Banes key off of Humanity, so having high Humanity makes most of them laughable without any additional need to offset them.<br /> <br /> Low Humanity vampires are going to find Banes worth it because it helps protect them from dropping to unplayable by making whatever thing they keep doing that drops their Humanity not do that any more. The Banes suck, but your low Humanity was already a problem and most of them are mitigated the same way as dealing with the universal Banes (avoidance, or using Disciplines to get around them).<br /> <br /> It's vampires in the middle (though were a lot of people default to playing, which might make Banes seem weird to consider) are the ones where there isn't much appeal. If they're not doing things that would drop them lower, Banes to protect them from that doesn't have a lot of a point. If they're not aiming for high Humanity, the bonuses for doing so aren't worth it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:22:13-07:00","id":1220647,"title":"","content":"I usualy play in the middle probaly why I dont see apeal then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}